1
00:00:01,270 --> 00:00:08,150
The new morning we've finally found

2
00:00:01,270 --> 00:00:08,150
Yatto mitsuketa atarashii asa wa

3
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:12,190
is being hampered by the past.

4
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:12,190
Tsukihi ga jama wo suru

5
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:17,660
What we chased after wasn't the future,

6
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:17,660
Mukau saki wa tsugi ja nakute

7
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:21,490
but the past so full of remorse.

8
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:21,490
Sugi bakari oikaketa

9
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:27,960
The ruthless memories won't stop playing;

10
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:27,960
Nariyamanai yousha nai omoide tachi wa

11
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:32,050
they won't be forgiving us for a long time.

12
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:32,050
Yurushite kuresou nimonai

13
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:37,890
It's about now that a teardrop

14
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:37,890
Sorosoro kana tesaguri tsukareta hoho wo

15
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:42,560
beings to roll down my fatigued cheeks.

16
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:42,560
Kattou ga koboreochiru

17
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:47,810
Will this rain ever stop?

18
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:47,810
Ame wa itsuka yamunodeshouka

19
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:53,030
I've been freezing for a long time.

20
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:53,030
Zuibun nagai aida tsumetai

21
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:58,320
Why does the rain continue to fix on me?

22
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:58,320
Ame wa doushite boku wo erabuno

23
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,080
I wonder if it could embrace me.

24
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,080
Tsutsumarete iikana

25
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:07,870
Today, the rain falls again;

26
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:07,870
Ame wa yamu koto wo shirazuni

27
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:13,090
endlessly it falls knowing no end.

28
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:13,090
Kyou mo furitsuzukukeredo

29
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:18,130
We nestle close to each other to share the warmth

30
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:18,130
Sotto sashidashita kasa no naka de

31
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:29,850
under this umbrella, you gently held out to me.

32
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:29,850
Nukumori ni yorisoinagara

33
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:49,370
The Führer President has returned?!

34
00:01:51,460 --> 00:01:54,210
I heard he destroyed a tank from Briggs at the main gate.

35
00:01:54,420 --> 00:01:57,510
That'll show those monkeys from Briggs!

36
00:01:57,510 --> 00:01:59,220
Let's gather the rest of the soldiers.

37
00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:00,720
We need to recapture mission headquarters!

38
00:02:01,140 --> 00:02:02,010
Yeah!

39
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:04,720
The Führer President is at the main gate?

40
00:02:08,890 --> 00:02:09,940
Oh.

41
00:02:10,810 --> 00:02:13,400
It's my first time seeing him with my own eyes.

42
00:02:17,190 --> 00:02:22,070
So he's the one who ripped off my granddaughter's arm...!

43
00:02:22,090 --> 00:02:25,090
Eternal Leave

44
00:02:22,090 --> 00:02:25,090
Eternal Leave

45
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:28,910
I see.

46
00:02:29,460 --> 00:02:34,500
So you were planning on sacrificing all the civilians
so that you high-level officials would gain immortality,

47
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:37,210
and unify the world.

48
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:43,090
Is Führer President Bradley doing everything
even with the knowledge of what you all are up to?

49
00:02:43,090 --> 00:02:46,010
He's the leader of this country,
and was made for that purpose.

50
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:49,520
Why are you hesitating?!

51
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:51,520
We're planning on creating a world without war!

52
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:54,150
So you're saying the world should be destroyed once for that purpose?

53
00:02:58,610 --> 00:03:00,740
It's not destruction, but rather regeneration.

54
00:03:01,110 --> 00:03:04,620
It's the 'reconstruction' stage that you alchemists refer to.

55
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:07,950
The civilians aren't going to be given 'death'.

56
00:03:08,290 --> 00:03:11,120
They're going to receive the honor of living within us forever!

57
00:03:11,410 --> 00:03:14,130
And we're going to unify the world together!

58
00:03:14,750 --> 00:03:16,630
All is one, and one is all!

59
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:21,340
We, the chosen ones of Amestris, will become one and-

60
00:03:25,470 --> 00:03:27,140
You heard him.

61
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:28,520
What will you guys do?

62
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:31,520
They're trying to gain everything for themselves.

63
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:33,520
Are you just going to let him go?

64
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:36,560
C-Come along with me, you all.

65
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:39,480
If you do, I'll ask that man to-

66
00:03:45,450 --> 00:03:50,750
I'm a soldier, so I must obey the orders of my superiors.

67
00:03:51,450 --> 00:03:54,870
But to be honest, I don't know what to believe anymore...

68
00:03:55,750 --> 00:03:58,880
You're still hesitating in this situation?

69
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:04,090
Obeying a superior you can't even believe doesn't make you loyal.

70
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:06,340
You're just fooling yourself.

71
00:04:09,390 --> 00:04:10,770
Believe in yourselves.

72
00:04:12,390 --> 00:04:17,020
Just choose a way of living that won't shame your soul.

73
00:04:29,410 --> 00:04:31,950
I have family in the city.

74
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:34,580
So do I.

75
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:35,750
I, too, as well.

76
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:54,640
Brigadier General,

77
00:04:55,730 --> 00:04:57,770
this is our answer.

78
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:06,030
Mission headquarters, what's the situation?

79
00:05:06,450 --> 00:05:08,200
Not too great.

80
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:11,240
The Central Soldiers have begun to recover in several areas.

81
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:12,410
Where are you right now, General?

82
00:05:12,830 --> 00:05:14,790
The Führer President's office.

83
00:05:14,790 --> 00:05:15,750
And the survivors?

84
00:05:16,870 --> 00:05:19,920
We haven't been able to get in touch with our men who are around the office.

85
00:05:20,460 --> 00:05:23,800
There's a high possibility that there are many Central Soldiers surrounding it.

86
00:05:24,630 --> 00:05:25,920
Roger.

87
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:27,800
If things get dangerous over there, run.

88
00:05:28,970 --> 00:05:30,640
Just leave me behind.

89
00:05:32,970 --> 00:05:34,020
Aye, Ma'am.

90
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:38,690
Now, this place has become filled with enemies again.

91
00:05:39,270 --> 00:05:43,730
It's only a matter of time until the Central Soldiers form up and storm this place.

92
00:05:44,230 --> 00:05:45,610
Which means...

93
00:05:54,830 --> 00:05:56,370
After going down a bit,

94
00:05:56,370 --> 00:05:58,960
I'll dig a side tunnel as an escape route, just like I did when I came here.

95
00:05:59,330 --> 00:06:00,920
Escape...

96
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:02,000
Why don't we escape together?

97
00:06:02,750 --> 00:06:06,050
You all could probably use some time to recover and plan, couldn't you?

98
00:06:26,990 --> 00:06:28,400
He's close.

99
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:30,610
You think so too?

100
00:06:30,610 --> 00:06:33,280
You two can sense him?

101
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:35,030
It's more of a "bad feeling".

102
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:39,910
Like the feeling you get when a bad scar starts aching.

103
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:05,690
Oh my, do I have guests?

104
00:07:05,690 --> 00:07:07,900
I'm a little nervous.

105
00:07:13,320 --> 00:07:14,070
Who are you?!

106
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:15,990
Me?

107
00:07:16,910 --> 00:07:18,580
Hmm...

108
00:07:18,580 --> 00:07:21,250
The man who created King Bradley...

109
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:25,380
...perhaps?

110
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:27,880
The Führer President...

111
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:34,840
Which means you're on their side.

112
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:38,100
Huh? You're...

113
00:07:38,100 --> 00:07:43,350
I thought you were at the radio station,
but you actually took the effort to come here.

114
00:07:43,350 --> 00:07:47,360
Thanks for giving me one less thing to do, Mustang.

115
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:54,240
Guys, entertain them for a while.

116
00:07:57,870 --> 00:07:59,580
Who the hell are they?!

117
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:01,370
Dolls?!

118
00:08:01,370 --> 00:08:02,460
No...

119
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:05,380
Their movements clearly differ from the dolls!

120
00:08:05,380 --> 00:08:09,630
They're men who might have become King Bradley.

121
00:08:12,090 --> 00:08:14,180
They were gathered as soon as they were born,

122
00:08:14,510 --> 00:08:17,970
and they were given special education and training

123
00:08:17,970 --> 00:08:21,560
for the sole purpose of becoming the Führer President.

124
00:08:22,730 --> 00:08:28,150
And with the twelfth experiment, King Bradley was born.

125
00:08:29,730 --> 00:08:31,690
So these are...!

126
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:34,490
The leftovers.

127
00:08:34,990 --> 00:08:39,330
Despite that, they've been training for battle all this time.

128
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:48,040
Although they're not as powerful as King Bradley,

129
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:49,790
they're pretty good.

130
00:09:15,450 --> 00:09:16,150
Damn...

131
00:09:16,820 --> 00:09:18,410
...those rebels...!

132
00:09:20,490 --> 00:09:22,870
Shit, I passed out.

133
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:27,000
Captain!

134
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:28,620
That's right...

135
00:09:29,830 --> 00:09:32,550
If I were to pull it out, I'd probably die from blood loss.

136
00:09:38,970 --> 00:09:40,140
Bradley...!

137
00:09:49,650 --> 00:09:51,520
That was close, old man!

138
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:53,020
It was an accident, youn-

139
00:09:53,020 --> 00:09:53,940
It wasn't on purpose!

140
00:09:57,990 --> 00:09:58,650
You-

141
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:15,960
As I thought, prey like you gets my heart pumping faster.

142
00:10:24,390 --> 00:10:28,140
I'm surprised you put up such a good fight despite being more aged than I.

143
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:29,690
But...!

144
00:10:29,850 --> 00:10:31,730
It ends here!

145
00:10:37,860 --> 00:10:38,490
Gramps!

146
00:10:48,750 --> 00:10:50,410
The prince from Xing, eh?

147
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:52,670
Dammit, Lin!

148
00:10:52,670 --> 00:10:54,670
Quit taking over without asking!

149
00:10:55,630 --> 00:11:00,010
You're just like the girl who cut her own arm off.

150
00:11:00,010 --> 00:11:05,430
Just like her, you endanger your life for something you can't throw away.

151
00:11:05,970 --> 00:11:07,560
Young master...

152
00:11:07,560 --> 00:11:10,770
I can no longer fight. Just throw me away...

153
00:11:10,770 --> 00:11:12,100
Quit joking!

154
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:14,310
Are you telling me to become a man like him?!

155
00:11:15,310 --> 00:11:17,610
A king exists for his people.

156
00:11:17,610 --> 00:11:20,150
Without his people, there is no king.

157
00:11:20,150 --> 00:11:23,700
He's planning on abandoning the people of his country.

158
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:27,740
That's not someone I want to become!

159
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:32,710
A man unworthy of being called 'king', huh...

160
00:11:33,370 --> 00:11:35,880
Then we must defeat him.

161
00:11:36,670 --> 00:11:37,800
Don't speak!

162
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:38,800
Take a break!

163
00:11:51,060 --> 00:11:52,690
I agree.

164
00:11:52,690 --> 00:11:53,940
I'll take a break...

165
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:55,940
I shall rest.

166
00:11:58,570 --> 00:12:00,480
Harden, Greed!

167
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:01,820
Protect the young master's body!

168
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:03,200
R-Right!

169
00:12:06,070 --> 00:12:06,870
Young master...

170
00:12:07,490 --> 00:12:09,450
Become king.

171
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:16,630
It's time for this old geezer to begin his eternal rest!

172
00:12:18,090 --> 00:12:21,300
Idiot!!{make sure you time both of these; it's important! ~koki}

173
00:12:18,090 --> 00:12:21,300
Idiot!!

174
00:12:23,760 --> 00:12:25,970
You're coming to hell with me,

175
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:28,600
Bradley!!

176
00:12:43,490 --> 00:12:48,820
I can't give him a single wound, even by risking my life?

177
00:12:51,540 --> 00:12:52,660
Young master...

178
00:12:53,410 --> 00:12:56,710
I'm so sorry...

179
00:13:00,670 --> 00:13:04,420
Even if you possess the eyes of God,

180
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:09,930
you can't possibly dodge an attack coming from somewhere you can't see!

181
00:13:12,680 --> 00:13:16,310
Old man, I'll... be going...

182
00:13:16,310 --> 00:13:20,690
to hell with you...

183
00:13:23,070 --> 00:13:26,650
I'm so grateful...

184
00:13:53,970 --> 00:13:56,020
Grandpa!!!

185
00:14:07,950 --> 00:14:08,950
Jesus!

186
00:14:08,950 --> 00:14:11,780
First you get stuck in a ditch,
then you ram into a lightpost?!

187
00:14:11,780 --> 00:14:13,950
You really suck at driving!

188
00:14:13,950 --> 00:14:15,120
Shut it!

189
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:18,910
Be thankful that we were able to get this far in a beat up car like that!

190
00:14:18,910 --> 00:14:21,250
We've come this far! Stop fighting!

191
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:25,210
Anyway, we need to hurry up and find a place where we can get underground.

192
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:28,880
That's...

193
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:35,810
Colonel Mustang?

194
00:14:35,810 --> 00:14:37,640
I hope they're doing well.

195
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:39,560
Brother...

196
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:42,560
Let's hurry!

197
00:14:51,610 --> 00:14:58,040
How non-human can your movements get?!

198
00:15:33,490 --> 00:15:35,780
Colonel, your back is wide open.

199
00:15:35,780 --> 00:15:38,740
There's someone I've entrusted my back to, so yeah.

200
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:44,630
The gate of truth.

201
00:15:45,920 --> 00:15:48,750
Human transmutation, a taboo in alchemy.

202
00:15:49,420 --> 00:15:54,010
Alchemists who try it end up opening the gate of truth,

203
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:56,970
paying a befitting toll.

204
00:15:58,640 --> 00:16:04,190
So that's how the Elric Brothers sacrificed their bodies?

205
00:16:05,060 --> 00:16:05,650
Did you do it too?

206
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:11,280
They took a bit of my insides.

207
00:16:12,530 --> 00:16:15,070
But what I learned from all that,

208
00:16:15,570 --> 00:16:21,330
is that human transmutation never works.

209
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:29,380
Oh my, soldiers like yourselves probably aren't interested in tales like these.

210
00:16:30,090 --> 00:16:31,260
Not true.

211
00:16:32,170 --> 00:16:37,800
Humans who have opened the gate of truth are the "human sacrifices" they speak of.

212
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:42,020
You may have a handhold in finding out what they are up to.

213
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:46,100
So you all had someone you wanted to see again,

214
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:51,940
even if you had to open the gate of truth and sacrifice your body.

215
00:16:55,820 --> 00:16:56,740
What about you?

216
00:16:57,950 --> 00:17:01,700
Do you have someone that you'd give up anything for just to see again?

217
00:17:03,290 --> 00:17:05,790
Now that's something that means nothing to a soldier.

218
00:17:06,620 --> 00:17:08,750
Having regret for the deceased is pointless.

219
00:17:09,290 --> 00:17:11,750
We fight in order to keep them alive.

220
00:17:13,010 --> 00:17:14,630
That's true.

221
00:17:15,170 --> 00:17:16,220
But...

222
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:19,850
...I feel like I understand something now.

223
00:17:22,140 --> 00:17:24,350
Edward Elric.

224
00:17:24,350 --> 00:17:29,230
When I first met him, I threatened him and told him to tell me everything he knows,

225
00:17:29,230 --> 00:17:34,860
but that boy didn't say a word about his old friend having been taken hostage.

226
00:17:35,440 --> 00:17:36,570
Just one line:

227
00:17:37,780 --> 00:17:39,490
"Please try to realize."

228
00:17:40,490 --> 00:17:44,040
Those eyes were different from those of us soldiers,

229
00:17:44,040 --> 00:17:49,290
or even those of State Alchemists,
who are referred to as the dogs of the military.

230
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:56,880
If I had to say, they were eyes that didn't want to lose anything important to them again no matter what...

231
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:01,640
Eyes of an unreasonable child?

232
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:08,350
I'd be lying if I said that those straightforward eyes didn't move my heart.

233
00:18:09,350 --> 00:18:16,280
But will those naïvely honest feelings of his
find a way out of the difficulty in this fight,

234
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:18,360
or will they come back to harm him?

235
00:18:20,910 --> 00:18:22,530
There.

236
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:25,580
Let us begin.

237
00:18:31,130 --> 00:18:32,670
Number 16,

238
00:18:32,670 --> 00:18:33,920
Number 17,

239
00:18:34,130 --> 00:18:35,920
Number 21,

240
00:18:36,090 --> 00:18:39,430
Number 23, Number 26.

241
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:41,050
Come here.

242
00:18:43,970 --> 00:18:44,930
What?!

243
00:18:49,140 --> 00:18:52,190
Here we go!

244
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:06,370
What did you do?!

245
00:19:06,370 --> 00:19:09,910
This is just the first step.

246
00:19:09,910 --> 00:19:16,590
Do you know how many alchemy research facilities under direct control of the Führer President exist in Central?

247
00:19:18,090 --> 00:19:21,340
There should be four that are currently being used...

248
00:19:21,590 --> 00:19:22,510
No!

249
00:19:26,010 --> 00:19:27,680
Research Laboratory 5...

250
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:29,310
There are five!

251
00:19:30,100 --> 00:19:33,980
A transmutation circle with five points!

252
00:19:34,690 --> 00:19:41,030
Could it be that the curving underground path was a circle that connects the research facilities?!

253
00:19:55,750 --> 00:19:56,590
What?!

254
00:20:00,710 --> 00:20:02,930
What's wrong, Mr. Heinkel?

255
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,360
Izumi.

256
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:26,200
Yeah.

257
00:20:27,030 --> 00:20:29,330
Seems like this is a good spot.

258
00:20:31,790 --> 00:20:34,870
I'm going to dig a hole for escape purposes in this wall.

259
00:20:34,870 --> 00:20:36,330
Stand back.

260
00:20:36,330 --> 00:20:37,880
Then this is where we say goodbye.

261
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:43,800
We still need to remain here and fight.

262
00:20:44,510 --> 00:20:48,220
From here on out is probably the enemy's backbone.

263
00:20:48,220 --> 00:20:52,020
We can't just let our chance to ambush them go to waste.

264
00:20:52,930 --> 00:20:54,390
You...

265
00:21:01,020 --> 00:21:02,530
Thanks for all your help.

266
00:21:04,570 --> 00:21:06,660
We're in your debt, Izumi Curtis.

267
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:09,410
I should be saying that, Major General Arm-

268
00:21:40,440 --> 00:21:41,320
What?!

269
00:21:55,620 --> 00:21:56,830
Alphonse!

270
00:21:58,500 --> 00:21:59,460
Izumi!

271
00:22:01,840 --> 00:22:03,630
Izumi!!

272
00:22:12,180 --> 00:22:14,350
F-Fullmetal...!

273
00:22:22,860 --> 00:22:27,360
Dammit...!!

274
00:22:39,290 --> 00:22:42,840
Ever since that day passed,

275
00:22:39,290 --> 00:22:42,840
Ano hi kara zutto

276
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:47,090
I promised myself that I'd never cry.

277
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:47,090
Nakanaito kimetekitakedo

278
00:22:47,630 --> 00:22:52,640
But even while I hoarded up the pain,

279
00:22:47,630 --> 00:22:52,640
Itami wo kasanetemo

280
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:57,750
there was something I couldn't forgive myself for.

281
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:57,750
Nanika wo yurusezu ni ita

282
00:22:59,230 --> 00:23:01,190
I'll never be able

283
00:22:59,230 --> 00:23:01,190
Mou modorenai

284
00:23:01,190 --> 00:23:03,690
to return to those days.

285
00:23:01,190 --> 00:23:03,690
Ikutsumo no hibi

286
00:23:03,690 --> 00:23:08,780
I'm still powerless.

287
00:23:03,690 --> 00:23:08,780
Boku wa mada nanimo dekizuni

288
00:23:08,780 --> 00:23:14,030
I watch as the shards of memories disappear, one by one;

289
00:23:08,780 --> 00:23:14,030
Kimi no ita kioku no kakera

290
00:23:14,030 --> 00:23:19,900
memories of when you were still with me.

291
00:23:14,030 --> 00:23:19,900
Mata hitotsu kieteyuku

292
00:23:20,580 --> 00:23:22,920
I long to become

293
00:23:20,580 --> 00:23:22,920
Kyou yori motto

294
00:23:22,920 --> 00:23:25,670
stronger than I am now,

295
00:23:22,920 --> 00:23:25,670
Tsuyoku naritai

296
00:23:25,670 --> 00:23:30,810
so that my voice will eventually reach you.

297
00:23:25,670 --> 00:23:30,810
Kono koe ga itsuka todokuyouni

298
00:23:30,810 --> 00:23:33,180
If the wind happens to stop

299
00:23:30,810 --> 00:23:33,180
Arukitsuzukete

300
00:23:33,180 --> 00:23:35,890
in the midst of my long journey,

301
00:23:33,180 --> 00:23:35,890
Kaze ga yandara

302
00:23:35,890 --> 00:23:40,600
I'll look up at the sky in search of you.

303
00:23:35,890 --> 00:23:40,600
Kimi wo sagashite sora miageruyo

304
00:23:41,350 --> 00:23:47,940
Beyond the daybreak, a ray of light breaks free.

305
00:23:41,350 --> 00:23:47,940
Yoake no saki ni hikari ga sasuyo

306
00:23:49,110 --> 00:23:53,490
A rainbow spans across the sky.

307
00:23:49,110 --> 00:23:53,490
Niji ga kakaruyo

308
00:23:59,910 --> 00:24:03,790
Anger is born at the extremities of sorrow,

309
00:24:03,790 --> 00:24:08,210
and when two souls dwell within a single body,

310
00:24:08,210 --> 00:24:10,760
the annihilations begins.

311
00:24:12,120 --> 00:24:16,680
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

312
00:24:16,680 --> 00:24:21,200
Episode 58, Sacrifices.

313
00:24:16,700 --> 00:24:21,200
Sacrifices

314
00:24:21,850 --> 00:24:27,110
Continuing to protect even after death is their long-cherished plan.
